1
00:05:15,789 --> 00:05:21,789
When America marched off to war the women marched into the
factory. From then on...nothing was the same.

2
00:10:31,578 --> 00:10:37,578
Swing Shift is a drama, romance, war film directed by Jonathan Demme.

3
00:15:47,368 --> 00:15:53,368
In 1941 America, Kay and her husband are happy enough
until he enlists after Pearl Harbor.

4
00:21:03,157 --> 00:21:09,157
Against his wishes, she takes a job at the local aircraft plant
where she meets Hazel, the singer from across the way.

5
00:26:18,947 --> 00:26:24,947
The two soon become firm friends and with the other
girls become increasingly expert workers.

6
00:31:34,736 --> 00:31:40,736
As the war drags on, Kay finally dates her trumpet-playing
foreman and life gets more complicated.

7
00:36:50,526 --> 00:36:56,526
Kay Walsh, played by Goldie Hawn.

8
00:42:06,315 --> 00:42:12,315
Lucky Lockhart, played by Kurt Russell.

9
00:47:22,105 --> 00:47:28,105
Hazel Zanussi, played by Christine Lahti.

10
00:52:37,894 --> 00:52:43,894
Biscuits Toohey, played by Fred Ward.

11
00:57:53,684 --> 00:57:59,684
Jack Walsh, played by Ed Harris.

12
01:03:09,473 --> 01:03:15,473
Annie, played by Sudie Bond.

13
01:08:25,263 --> 01:08:31,263
Swing Shift is a 1984 American romantic drama directed by Jonathan Demme,
and produced by and starring Goldie Hawn, with Kurt Russell.

14
01:13:41,052 --> 01:13:47,052
It also features Christine Lahti, Fred Ward, Ed Harris and
Holly Hunter, in one of her earlier movie roles.

15
01:18:56,842 --> 01:19:02,842
The film was a box office bomb, grossing just $6.6
million against its $15 million budget.

16
01:24:12,631 --> 01:24:18,631
Lahti earned a nomination for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress.

17
01:29:28,421 --> 01:29:34,421
The film explores themes of world war ii, home
front, riveter, arms industry, 1940s.

18
01:34:44,210 --> 01:34:50,210
The tone is emotional.
